comments.body:
@participant2 Thanks for the quick response. Yes it's for existing repos but I've not needed to add a new repo so can't comment on that. 

I'd appreciate a revert and re-deploy if possible as it's currently stopping me from running updates via puppet across my whole estate. I understand the reasoning behind the repo labels change and of course it would be great to resolve both but for now a revert and redeploy would aid me greatly. 

Yes running `sudo apt-get update --allow-releaseinfo-change` does fix the issue for us. I wanted to add this to my pupup command but I can't pupup to get it changed in the pupup file so  I would need to manually run the command per server.
